# What `bash dot sync` links into the project: one origin::destination per line,
# destinations relative to the project, outside .dot/ and .git/. The first line
# naming a destination takes precedense.
#
# Origin shortcuts:
#   @AGENTS.md                      One of dotdot's top-level docs
#   @dotdotSkills, @dotdotAgents    Each of dotdot's skills and agents, linked one
#                                   by one into the destination directory
#   @pluginsSkills, @pluginsAgents  The same for every plugin's skills/ and agents/
#   @module.<name>.<path>           A path in a dotdot module: @module.notes.skills
#   @plugin.<owner>.<name>.<path>   A path in a plugin: @plugin.acme.tools.skills
#   <path>                          A path in dotdot; in a plugin's block, in that plugin
#
# Origin linking types:
#   ending with <destination>       Links it as is (a file, or a whole directory)
#   ending with /*                  Links each entry inside individually
#   starting with !                 Removes the link and keeps it unlinked
#
# Each plugin gets a block, written from its plugin.conf when it is added and
# dropped when it is removed; `bash dot sync --refresh <owner>/<name>` (and
# `plugins:update`) writes it afresh.

@AGENTS.md::AGENTS.md
@dotdotSkills::.claude/skills/
